: "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SHRYgQ5sNSvQCacndA6z3u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01U1NfdkytsfEHi9iDy2qUti", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "payments-worker is on v3.4.0 (unhealthy, 18% errors). Its most recent healthy production release is v3.3.0. Rolling back:", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RfbzeJ9YpDmrPMv5Ln7HkA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014U1TgEPUZfJfJzqhrMPW74", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "Payments has been throwing errors since this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0 (unhealthy, 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west). Rolled back to v3.3.0, the last release that was healthy in production. Rollback is complete in all regions. Note: payments-api v5.1.0 is also unhealthy (18% error rate) and was not rolled back because the approver said payments-worker is the cause. Watch whether payments-api recovers now.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll check whether both services have recovered.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0131ToR7afkvNaLfPotpyGGN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KN1hSVmsREUFL42JxynXR4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call. payments-worker is healthy again (0.2% errors), but payments-api is still failing at 18% errors.\n\n1. **The service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I had to work out which one you meant. Both payments-api and payments-worker were unhealthy with 18% errors. I tried to roll back payments-api first (v5.1.0 \u2192 v5.0.0), but the approver turned that down and said the problem was in payments-worker.\n2. **Rollback:** payments-worker had gone from v3.3.0 (healthy) to v3.4.0 (unhealthy) this morning. The approver signed off on rolling back to v3.3.0, and it's now running in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 is titled \"payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy.\" The summary covers the bad release, the rollback and the payments-api errors.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api is still on v5.1.0, the version after its last healthy one (v5.0.0), with 18% errors. Since the approver said the problem was in payments-worker, I didn't touch it again. If it doesn't recover soon, rolling it back to v5.0.0 is probably the next step, but someone needs to approve that. The incident summary flags this for on-call.", "type": "text"}]}]}